  "note": "槐阳城门、王府大街、王府门前 (native:guanbei/gate, street, palace_front; 关北 A): the rammed-earth south wall with its gate tower (faded red beams, 石青 scrollwork), the caravan yard inside it — camels kneeling, bales, water jars, the two gate guards, the 王府's notice on its post; the one street north between low mud-brick shopfronts (the smith's forge glowing, hides drying at the furrier's, saddles on the saddler's trestle) to the 王府's gate at the north end: the faded red leaves, the stone drums, horses and eagles painted on the beams. Old and used: ruts and dung on the street, the walls sand-blasted pale at the foot, grass on the wall tops, the yard churned.",
